  "findings": [
    "Only the two ordinary-state rect fill producers were changed, at current state.rs:7332/7412, plus existing fill_attributes visibility. Coordinates, stroke and every other argument remain identical. Java EntityImageStateEmptyDescription/EntityImageState \u2192 DriverRectangleSvg \u2192 fillMe source hashes match the pin.",
    "Fresh state-fill whole cohort is1\u21928/24 valid; zero errors, panics, malformed outputs or lost passes. The two ordinary rectangle branches serialize alpha00/01/7f/fe/ff and #9b4 paint exactly: none; #7A3C91 with opacity0.00392/0.49804/0.99608; opaque omits opacity; short hex becomes #99BB44. Empty-description dimensions still differ, so matching paint is bounded support.",
    "Both ordinary transparent inputs emit white #FFFFFF instead of Java fill=none. state.rs::resolve_state_paint passes the name through sequence::resolve_color, whose unknown-name fallback is white before fill_attributes sees it. RebeccaPurple resolves to Rust #663399 versus Java #FFFFFF in both branches. Whole failure is preserved, including named-color acceptance differences.",
    "Unrouted paths remain: emit_autonomous_scope_entities ordinary nested rectangles (4032), start/end (3802/3820), choice (3840), fork/join (3866), history/deep-history (3888), border entry/exit/normal shapes (3946/3955); empty concurrent rectangle4326; autonomous composite header4400; root cluster header5488. Main render branches also bypass shared paint for initial/final ellipses6958/6997/7063/7110, choice7140, fork/join7167, history7017/7199 and deep-history7239, and oracle polygon/path passthrough1600/1632/1646. Fixed none/stroke-only surfaces are not alpha claims. Full source census and paint projections are retained.",
    "Composite/concurrent probes emit raw #7a3c917f with no opacity for header and nested normal rectangle, while Java uses #7A3C91 fill-opacity=0.49804. Choice selects the skin fill in Rust where Java uses #F1F1F1. Fork/join fixed bar paints match in these probes but still bypass the serializer. History/deep-history have missing shape/name differences. Named start/end probe follows a wrong Rust dispatch/render path. No scope expansion or production repair was attempted."
  ],
